861060505392001-b965b913-5a88-4039-839d-f974c21cb80e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"be254fffe1917f102bd0af239b89590277418fc638288ab16e92917004a3ed8a","event_uuid":"29f6cee0-4cc8-4ee8-99e1-d9b8461b2991","position":{"commit_sha":"1fa49c82bc9dbfbbdf21beb8bde5690d0ea835c2","position":"1787863495612720001-29f6cee0-4cc8-4ee8-99e1-d9b8461b2991"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-247_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"41c69740-e628-4506-a328-65f32258a98e","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Second independent victim of the same missing-.git mechanism, observed on the same live server:\n\n    reconcile {\"mode\": \"dry-run\"}\n      -> {\"error\": \"command_failed\",\n          \"message\": \"reconcile (dry-run) failed (exit 1): ERROR: reconciler process failed\n           before finalization: Command '['git', '-C', '/app', 'hash-object', '-w',\n           '--stdin']' returned non-zero exit status 128.\"}\n\nreconcile dry-run is documented as non-mutating and always available, and it fails for the same\nreason as review_plan/verify_completion: /app has no git object DB, so \nexits 128. This widens the blast radius beyond the LLM gates and is covered by AC4 (a real git\nobject DB at the repo root) and AC5 (a deploy-time health check).","timestamp":1787815565502359559},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Third victim of the same missing-.git mechanism, same live server:\n\n    review_code {\"base\": \"HEAD~1\", \"head\": \"HEAD\"}\n      -> {\"error\": \"llm_unavailable\",\n          \"message\": \"git diff HEAD~1...HEAD failed: warning: Not a git repository.\n           Use --no-index to compare two paths outside a working tree ...\"}\n\nConfirmed blast radius on the deployed server, all from /app having no git object DB:\n  - review_plan       (default attested source) - fails\n  - verify_completion (default attested source) - fails\n  - review_code                                  - fails\n  - reconcile         (dry-run, documented non-mutating/always-available) - fails\n  - attach_commits                               - cannot resolve any SHA\nOnly source=local variants run, and a local verdict is never signed.","timestamp":1787815738422559670},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Phase 1 EXIT — root cause confirmed, mechanism and legitimacy both proven\n\n### Root cause (a changeable artifact)\n\nThe mcp image never contains git metadata, so no attested gate can resolve a ref:\n\n- `.dockerignore:5` excludes `.git`.\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp:42` is `COPY . /app`, with `WORKDIR /app` at `:33`.\n\nSo `/app` is a plain source copy. `_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:293` raises\n`cannot resolve ref 'origin/main' to a commit in '.'` because there is no repository to\nresolve against.\n\n### Runtime proof (dynamic claim, observed executing — not read from source)\n\n    docker exec compose-mcp-1 sh -c 'ls -d /app/.git; cat /app/.deployed_ref; echo $REBAR_ROOT; pwd'\n      ls: cannot access '/app/.git': No such file or directory\n      d4a0a2a44 (feat/gerrit-ci-verified-gate)\n      REBAR_ROOT=[<unset>]\n      /app\n\n`.deployed_ref` is a TEXT MARKER standing in for a clone. `REBAR_ROOT` is unset, so the repo\nroot resolves to the working directory `/app`, which has no `.git`. That is the whole\nmechanism: every attested-source gate (`review_plan`, `verify_completion`, `review_code`,\n`reconcile`) fails identically, and `attach_commits` can resolve no SHA.\n\n**Discriminating detail:** `source: \"local\"` DOES run — which rules out \"the gates are broken\"\nand isolates the fault to the attested-source path specifically, i.e. to the missing repo\nrather than to the gate code. But a local verdict is never signed, so it cannot satisfy a gate.\n\n### Legitimacy: incomplete-implementation (NOT feature-request)\n\nCited design authority — **ADR 0104 §3**:\n\n> For the two op-cert kinds minted via MCP (plan-review at claim, completion-verifier at close\n> — ADR 0049) to be **enforceable**, the MCP server signs them under the box's **EXISTING**\n> opcert signing environment...\n\nThe capability was designed and approved with an operator ruling (2026-08-24, Option A). It was\nnever wired: the service shipped without a repo for the attested source to resolve against.\nThat is a defect-class miss, not a feature request.\n\n### Net effect\n\nNo attestation can be earned through the live MCP server, so no task/story/epic can be closed\nthrough it without a force — which agents are forbidden to use. The MCP surface is therefore\nunable to complete the very workflow AGENTS.md directs agents to route through it.\n\n### Attribution — by SCOPE OF WORK, not by introducing commit\n\nNo commit broke this; the service never had a repo, so `git blame` has nothing to find. The\nscope-of-work owner is **`fd4a-4e91-f179-4932`** (`cibophobic-holohedral-esok`,\n\"rebar-mcp HTTP transport service on the AWS box\"), the story that shipped the service and\nits Dockerfile. A reviewer of that story could plausibly have caught that a container with no\n`.git` cannot serve certified ops the ADR says it must — which is the test for a correct\nattribution target. Recorded here because the `caused_by` link form is gated on the target\nhaving a referencing commit and this is an omission.","timestamp":1787851646659272001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Phase 2 — fix pushed as Gerrit change 2271\n\n**Fix.** The entrypoint provisions a code checkout at `MCP_CODE_DIR` (default\n`/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code`) with `--filter=blob:none --single-branch --branch main`, and\n`REBAR_ROOT` points at it. Blobless because the gates fetch objects on demand and a full clone\nof this repo is prohibitively large. Backgrounded like the tickets clone so it cannot block\n`exec` past the 120s readiness deadline; until it converges the gates fail exactly as they do\ntoday, no worse. Presence requires a RESOLVABLE HEAD, not just `.git`, so a container killed\nmid-clone re-clones instead of being mistaken for converged — the lesson from\n`fathomable-yester-thrip`. `REBAR_ROOT`/`MCP_CODE_DIR` are set in BOTH docker-compose.yml and\n`mcp_run_new`, which the compose-parity test pins.\n\n**Test — held out, GREEN, and has teeth.**\n`test_the_code_root_is_provisioned_so_attested_gates_can_resolve_main` was written and confirmed\nRED (zero code clones executed; liveness anchor passing) BEFORE the fix, then moved out of the\nimplementing agent's worktree entirely — it was never visible to the fixer. Re-applied after:\nGREEN. Defect-seeded mutation (remove the `provision_code` call, i.e. re-introduce the exact\nroot cause) returns it to RED with the git-call list showing no clone. It asserts observable\nbehaviour — what the script EXECUTED — not the presence of a line, so it is not a\nchange-detector.\n\n**Scope & safety.** No existing test modified (the only test delta is the oracle). No new\ndependency; no `src/` or manifest change at all. The `rm -rf` guard was generalised rather than\nduplicated — both layers (absolute-non-`/` case guard, cd-relative glob) now live in the single\n`clear_dir` every caller uses, and it gained trailing-slash normalisation so the globs cannot\ndegenerate. The existing unsafe-dir tests still exercise it unmodified and pass. Lint,\ntypecheck, shellcheck clean; 50 tests in the affected files pass.\n\n**Step 7 parity sweep — the MCP server was the ONLY affected surface.** Both sibling containers\nrun attested gates and both were checked, not assumed:\n- **review-bot — N/A.** `gerrit_client.clone_change_ref` builds its own working tree per review\n  (`git init` + fetch of the change ref). It never relies on `/app`, and it demonstrably works.\n- **opcert_service — N/A.** `opcert_service/workspace.py` provisions an ephemeral clone per job\n  as a stated SECURITY property: \"the worker fetches authoritative state ITSELF — never trusts\n  the client... so review_plan / verify_completion read state the client cannot influence.\"\n\nBoth provision their own repository; the MCP server did not. That is the parity signature, and\nit is why this is a single-surface omission rather than a class.\n\n**Step 6 replication — NOT yet done, stated rather than implied.** The original report can only\nbe replicated against a DEPLOYED server, and 2271 has not merged or deployed. AC1-AC3 (a\n`review_plan` through the live endpoint returning a verdict and persisting a certified\nattestation) remain unverified until it lands. They are not ticked.\n\n**Residual risk.** A failed code clone degrades to today's behaviour — the gates error — because\nenforcement is out of scope by operator ruling. Accepted deliberately: gating promotion on a\nbackgrounded clone is what produced the rollback loop in `unfit-beneficial-whimbrel`.","timestamp":1787853604007650001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Change 2271 got LLM-Review -1, and the blocking finding is CORRECT\n\nRecording this against the fix rather than quietly amending, because the reviewer caught a\ndefect I introduced while fixing the original one.\n\n**The finding.** `provision_code` was placed INSIDE the `if [ -n \"\\${MCP_TICKETS_PAT:-}\" ]`\nguard, but `REBAR_ROOT` is exported UNCONDITIONALLY in all three declaration sites\n(Dockerfile.mcp ENV, docker-compose.yml, autodeploy.sh `mcp_run_new`). docker-compose.yml\ndocuments a blank PAT as a SUPPORTED state — \"BLANK IS FINE, the container still boots\". So on\na blank-PAT deployment my change pointed the single global repo-root override at a directory\nthat is never created. That is a NEW failure mode introduced by the fix, not the one it removes.\n\n**Why it happened.** I attached the code clone to the tickets credential because both use\n`MCP_TICKETS_URL`, and treated one URL as implying one guard. The two clones have genuinely\ndifferent credential needs: the TICKETS clone pushes and needs the PAT; the CODE clone is\nread-only against a repository that answers anonymously —\n`GET https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/info/refs?service=git-upload-pack` returns **HTTP 200**,\nwhich I have now verified rather than assumed. So the code clone needs no credential at all and\nmust not share the guard.\n\n**RED first, again.** `test_the_code_root_is_provisioned_even_without_a_tickets_pat` is written\nand confirmed RED for the right reason — with `pat=None` the recorded git-call list is `[]`,\nzero clones, while the liveness anchor still passes, so the script demonstrably ran and skipped\nthe work. It is held out of the fixing tree exactly as the first oracle was.\n\n**One existing test legitimately changes**, and it should be visible rather than buried:\n`test_no_pat_skips_the_clone_but_still_converges_the_store` asserts `not run.cloned`, and\n`Run.cloned` matches ANY clone. It was written when the tickets clone was the only clone. After\nthe fix a code clone DOES fire with no PAT, so the assertion is being narrowed to the tickets\nclone specifically (`--branch tickets`), with `tickets_cloned`/`code_cloned` replacing the\nambiguous `cloned`. That is a deliberate behaviour change being reflected in the test, not a\ntest bent to pass — flagging it so it gets scrutiny rather than a nod.\n\nThe seven advisory findings are all real test gaps in the same change (blank-PAT path,\ncode-clone failure posture, the mount-absent skip branch, the idempotent short-circuit) and are\nbeing closed in the same patchset.","timestamp":1787854595468949001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Answering the REBAR_ROOT blast-radius advisory (rather than letting it pass as non-blocking)\n\nThe reviewer's advisory is ACCURATE and worth an explicit answer, because `REBAR_ROOT` is a\nsingle global override and I am now setting it on a production container. Its consumers, read\noff main:\n\n- `src/rebar/config.py:310` — config DISCOVERY (where `rebar.toml` is found)\n- `src/rebar/config.py:531` — `reconciler_repo_root`\n- `src/rebar/_config_resolvers.py:240` — general `repo_root`\n- `src/rebar/_config_resolvers.py:387` — `resolve_run_root`, the workflow-run scratch base\n\n**The one that could have been serious is the ticket store, and it is safe — verified, not\nassumed.** If the tracker path derived from `repo_root`, pointing `REBAR_ROOT` at the code clone\nwould have silently MOVED the tickets store and re-created the empty-tracker outage this whole\nepic exists to fix. It does not: `config.tracker_dir()` reads `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` FIRST and\nreturns it verbatim before any `repo_root` call is reached (`config.py:138-156`), and compose\nsets that variable explicitly to `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`. So the store is unaffected by\nconstruction, not by luck.\n\n**Config discovery does change**, and this is the honest residual: `rebar.toml` will now be read\nfrom the clone rather than from `/app`. Both are the same repository, so they agree at boot —\nbut the clone is taken at container-start time and the image is built at deploy time, so a\ncontainer that starts appreciably later than its build could read a slightly newer `rebar.toml`\nthan the code it is running. In practice the two are minutes apart and `rebar.toml` changes\nrarely; the alternative — leaving `REBAR_ROOT` unset — leaves EVERY attested gate unusable,\nwhich is strictly worse. Recording it so the tradeoff is visible rather than discovered later.\n\nThe remaining consumers (`reconciler_repo_root`, `resolve_run_root`) are strictly IMPROVED by\nthe change: today they resolve against `/app`, which has no object DB at all, so anything\ndepending on them is already broken on this container.","timestamp":1787854749344876001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## CORRECTION: change 2271 was NECESSARY but NOT SUFFICIENT. This ticket is not fixed.\n\nI wrote that 2271 fixes the attested gates, pending only deployment. It is deployed, and they\nstill fail. Correcting that here rather than letting the earlier comment stand.\n\n### What 2271 did achieve — verified on the live container\n\n    REBAR_ROOT=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code\n    MCP_CODE_DIR=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code\n    git -C /var/gerrit/site/mcp-code rev-parse origin/main\n      -> 269f7b49c44fd87da2bf26f8f5d35ba6d9df6ad0\n    git -C /var/gerrit/site/mcp-code rev-parse main   -> same\n    origin -> https://github.com/navapbc/rebar.git [blob:none]\n\nThe repository is provisioned, healthy, and resolves BOTH refs. That half of the diagnosis was\nright and the fix works.\n\n### The remaining cause: the snapshot layer never consults REBAR_ROOT\n\n`src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:264` (and identically at `:503` and `:699`):\n\n    root = str(repo_root) if repo_root else \".\"\n\nWhen `repo_root` is `None` it falls back to the literal `\".\"` — the PROCESS CWD, which is\n`/app` in the container, and `/app` has no object DB because `.dockerignore` excludes `.git`.\nIt never asks the config layer.\n\nAnd none of the MCP LLM tools pass a `repo_root`: `_mcp_llm.py:116` (`review_code`), `:146`\n(`scan_spec`), `:196` (`verify_completion`) all call `rebar.llm.*` without one. So every\nattested-source tool takes the `None` -> `\".\"` path.\n\nDemonstrated directly, from a non-repo cwd with REBAR_ROOT set:\n\n    repo_root_or_none()  -> /Users/joeoakhart/71e7-codex-mcp-pat   (honours it correctly)\n    snapshot default     -> \".\"                                    (ignores it)\n\n### The experiment that settles it — and refutes the reported cause\n\nA parallel Copilot session retried `review_plan` with an EXPLICIT full SHA and got the same\nerror: `cannot resolve ref '269f7b49c44fd87da2bf26f8f5d35ba6d9df6ad0' to a commit in '.'`. It\nconcluded the server's clone is 'stale, disconnected, or configured differently'.\n\nThat conclusion is WRONG, and the SHA is what disproves it: it is exactly the commit I verified\n`/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code` resolves. A stale clone cannot explain failing to find a commit the\nclone demonstrably contains. Looking in the WRONG DIRECTORY explains it exactly — and the error\nmessage names that directory, `'.'`, not `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code`. The `'.'` was the tell all\nalong.\n\n### Class\n\nSame family as `damageable-huge-xiphosuran`: shipped code bypassing rebar's own configured\nresolver and substituting a hardcoded default. That one is `tracker_dir`; this is `repo_root`.\n\nThis ticket stays IN PROGRESS. AC1-AC3 remain unticked, correctly.","timestamp":1787859682124446001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Fix authored — the snapshot layer now honours the CONFIGURED repo root\n\n**RED first, reproducing the production error byte-for-byte.**\n`tests/unit/test_snapshot_honours_configured_repo_root.py` builds a real one-commit repo, points\n`REBAR_ROOT` at it, `chdir`s to a directory that is NOT a repo, and calls\n`resolve_ref(\"main\", fetch=False)` with no explicit root — the exact shape of the deployed\ncontainer (cwd `/app` with no object DB, `REBAR_ROOT=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code`). It failed with:\n\n    SnapshotRefError: cannot resolve ref 'main' to a commit in '.'\n\nwhich is the SAME message, naming the same `'.'`, that the live server produced. That is a\nfaithful reproduction rather than an approximation of one.\n\n**The fix.** A single `_resolved_root()` seam in `_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py` replaces the three\n`str(repo_root) if repo_root else \".\"` fallbacks (in `resolve_ref`, `materialize`, and\n`materialize_tickets`). An explicit `repo_root` still WINS; only the `None` case changes, falling\nback to `repo_root_or_none()` (`REBAR_ROOT`, then the git toplevel of cwd) before `\".\"`.\n\n**A negative control guards the dangerous direction.**\n`test_an_explicit_repo_root_still_wins_over_the_environment` asserts that `REBAR_ROOT` does NOT\noverride an explicitly-passed root. Getting that backwards would be a worse bug than the one\nbeing fixed — silently reading a DIFFERENT tree than the caller named — so it is pinned rather\nthan left to reviewer attention.\n\n**Mutation-checked.** Reverting `_resolved_root` to return `\".\"` turns the reproduction RED again\nwith the identical error and leaves the negative control passing. `make lint` clean,\n`make typecheck` clean across 677 files.\n\n**Why a seam rather than three edits.** The three call sites had drifted into the same hardcoded\ndefault independently; a shared helper means the next snapshot entry point cannot reintroduce it\nby copy-paste, and the reasoning (with the outage that motivated it) lives in one docstring.\n\n**NOT YET DONE — the live-validation criterion.** This is authored and verified locally only. The\nnew mandatory AC requires `review_plan`/`scan_spec` to be OBSERVED returning a verdict through\n`https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp` after this lands and the container redeploys. That is\nprecisely the step I skipped when I claimed 2271 had fixed this ticket, so it is not being\nskipped again: the box stays unticked until a live call is made and its response recorded here.","timestamp":1787861060505392001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Fix pushed as Gerrit 2275 — and I MOVED it mid-flight, which is worth explaining\n\n**Where the fix landed, and why not where I first put it.** My first version added a helper to\n`_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py`, replacing its three `str(repo_root) if repo_root else \".\"`\nfallbacks. That was the deepest correct layer — and it would have FAILED CI.\n\nThat file sits at **exactly 800 LOC**, the locked hard cap. My version took it to **823**. Every\nlocal gate passed: `make lint` clean, `make typecheck` clean across 677 files, 882 targeted tests\ngreen. The module-size gate is a step in `_build-and-test.yml`, NOT a `make lint` target, so a\ngreen local run is entirely consistent with a commit CI rejects. I only checked because a\nparallel agent hit the identical trap on the same file an hour earlier and reported it.\n`pytest tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` is the local mirror; it is not in the default\nselection.\n\nThe file had no headroom for even a one-line import, and I declined to delete a blank line to fit\n— buying space with a cosmetic diff in a file at a hard limit is the exact pattern that had just\ngone wrong.\n\n**The relocation is better on the merits, not just a workaround.**\n`llm/gate_source.resolve_gate_handle` is documented as the function that applies 'the configured\ndefaults for `None`', and it ALREADY does exactly that for `ref` and `source`:\n\n    resolved_ref    = ref    or default_ref(repo_root)\n    resolved_source = source or default_source(repo_root)\n    repo_root       = snapshot_repo_root(repo_root)      # <- the third default it owed\n\nThe root was simply a default it forgot. It is also the single entry point every attested gate\npasses through, so one change covers `review_plan`, `scan_spec`, `verify_completion` and\n`review_code`. The helper itself lives beside `repo_root_or_none` in `_config_resolvers`, the\nmodule that already owns root resolution — so the config layer resolves and the snapshot layer\nconsumes, rather than the snapshot layer reaching sideways into config.\n\n**Evidence.** The original RED reproduced the production error byte-for-byte at the snapshot\nlayer (`cannot resolve ref 'main' to a commit in '.'`). After relocating I retargeted the test to\nthe layer actually changed and established teeth by mutation: replacing the new line with `pass`\nreturns it to RED, and the negative control (an explicit `repo_root` is never overridden by\n`REBAR_ROOT`) stays green — that direction would be worse than the bug, since a gate would verify\na different tree than the caller named and still sign an attestation saying otherwise.\n\nGates: lint clean, typecheck clean (677 files), **module-size gate 4 passed**, 129 tests across\ngate_source / plan-review / snapshot consumers.\n\n**Residual, not fixed here:** `repo_snapshot.py`'s bare-cwd fallback remains for non-gate callers.\nThat is the same class as `damageable-huge-xiphosuran` and is left to it rather than forced into\na file with zero headroom.\n\n**LIVE VALIDATION still unticked** — pending 2275 merging and the container redeploying.","timestamp":1787863495612720001}],"created_at":1787815136989669529,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2235fcfa-36c7-480f-8f56-ff1dcb5ff0ad","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"1f19-adf2-ffb2-4b09"},{"link_uuid":"61976199-d698-4438-a495-0a6390ec7757","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c67b-ece5-707e-460e"},{"link_uuid":"af8b2c05-0c68-43cf-a1c9-f19fee351b8b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d26a-8ffa-97cd-4b2a"},{"link_uuid":"de11f2d3-ed41-4cee-b7fa-0d8264f4b788","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fe1f-2566-59c6-4c8f"},{"link_uuid":"85442856-ac19-48e7-9156-808bab47b0af","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"66f0-ddc9-bf24-4fa3"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nEvery **attested-source** LLM gate operation fails on the LIVE MCP server\n(`https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp`, container `compose-mcp-1`, image\n`compose-mcp:9499312eb7b05dc3d75d39c23ab74a5b4afc26b5`).\n\nObserved 2026-08-27 against the live endpoint:\n\n```\nreview_plan       {\"ticket_id\": \"ruby-griffinish-goitered\"}\n  -> Error executing tool review_plan: cannot resolve ref 'origin/main' to a commit in '.'.\nreview_plan       {\"ticket_id\": \"...\", \"ref\": \"HEAD\"}\n  -> Error executing tool review_plan: cannot resolve ref 'HEAD' to a commit in '.'.\nverify_completion {\"ticket_id\": \"...\"}\n  -> Error executing tool verify_completion: cannot resolve ref 'origin/main' to a commit in '.'.\nreview_plan       {\"ticket_id\": \"...\", \"source\": \"local\"}   -> RUNS (P1/P2/P3 emitted)\n```\n\n## Mechanism\nThe container's repo root has **no git metadata at all**. Verified in-container:\n\n```\n$ docker exec compose-mcp-1 sh -c 'pwd; ls -d /app/.git; git -C /app rev-parse origin/main'\n/app\nls: cannot access '/app/.git': No such file or directory\nfatal: not a git repository (or any of the parent directories): .git\n```\n\n`docker inspect` confirms `WorkingDir=/app`, `Cmd=[\"rebar-mcp\"]`, and the env carries\n`REBAR_TRACKER_DIR=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets` but **no `REBAR_ROOT`** — so the repo root\nresolves to the cwd `/app`, which is a plain source copy, not a work tree. The image ships\n`/app/.deployed_ref` (`d4a0a2a44 (feat/gerrit-ci-verified-gate)`) as a text marker instead of a\nreal clone. `source=attested` pins a snapshot at `ref` against that root's object DB, so ref\nresolution fails before any LLM call.\n\nThe tracker itself is unaffected: it is an out-of-tree clone reached via `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`,\nso all non-git tools (create/show/search/list/comment/edit/link/claim/transition) work.\n\n## Impact\n`attested` is the DEFAULT source for both gate ops, and a `local`-source verdict is never\nsigned. So **no plan-review or completion attestation can be earned through the live MCP\nserver**, and consequently no `task`/`story`/`epic` can be closed through it while\n`verify.require_plan_review_for_close` is on — the only remaining path is `--force`, which\nagents are prohibited from using. Reproduced live: probe task `ruby-griffinish-goitered`\n(`c67b-ece5-707e-460e`) is stuck `in_progress` with\n`plan-review close gate: unsigned: no certified plan-review attestation`, and the prescribed\nremedy (`review-plan`) is the very operation that cannot run.\n\n## Reproduction\n1. Call `review_plan` on any claimable ticket through the live MCP endpoint with default args.\n2. Observe `cannot resolve ref 'origin/main' to a commit in '.'`.\n3. Repeat with `source: \"local\"` and observe it runs.\n\n## Fix\n\nProvision a real repository for the gate ops to resolve against, and point the repo root at it.\n\n**Why not the obvious alternatives.** Shipping `.git` in the image (removing the\n`.dockerignore:5` exclusion) bloats every layer and pins a main that goes stale the moment the\nimage is built — the gates need a ref that tracks main, not a frozen one. Re-using the tickets\nclone at `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` is tempting since `MCP_TICKETS_URL` is the SAME repository, but it\nconflates the code root with the tracker: two different lifetimes, two different refspecs, and\na reader can no longer tell which one a failure came from.\n\n**Shape.** `provision_store` gains a sibling that clones the CODE side into\n`/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code` — `--filter=blob:none --single-branch --branch main`, so it is a\nblobless clone that fetches objects on demand rather than materializing the history — and\n`REBAR_ROOT` is set to it (compose env + `mcp_run_new`, which must stay in parity). That root\ncarries `rebar.toml`, so config resolution moves from the source copy at `/app` to a real\ncheckout, which is strictly better: the two agree today, and a real root is what the config\nseam expects.\n\n**Ordering.** Like the tickets clone this is backgrounded, so it cannot block `exec` past the\nreadiness deadline. Until it converges the gates fail exactly as they do today — no worse.\n\n**Enforcement is OUT OF SCOPE** (operator ruling, 2026-08-27). This change makes the attested\ngates work; it does NOT add a deploy-time check that refuses to promote a container whose code\nroot failed to resolve. A failed code clone therefore degrades to today's behaviour — the\ngates error — rather than blocking the deploy. That is a deliberate boundary, not an oversight:\ngating promotion on a backgrounded clone is what produced the rollback loop in\n`unfit-beneficial-whimbrel`, and re-introducing it here would trade one outage shape for\nanother.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] AC1: `review_plan` with default arguments against the deployed MCP server returns a plan-review verdict (PASS/BLOCK/INDETERMINATE) rather than a ref-resolution error.\n- [ ] AC2: `verify_completion` with default arguments likewise returns a completion verdict.\n- [ ] AC3: A PASS from AC1 persists a signed plan-review attestation, so `plan_review_status` on that ticket reports `certified`.\n- [ ] AC4: The deployed container exposes a git object DB for the repo root reachable by the gate ops (a real clone at the repo root, or an explicit `REBAR_ROOT` pointing at one), verified by `git -C <root> rev-parse origin/main` succeeding inside the container.\n\n## Definition of Done\n- [ ] DD1: AC1-AC3 demonstrated against a deployed MCP server.\n\n## Scope boundaries (operator rulings, 2026-08-27)\n\n- **Enforcement is out of scope.** No deploy-time refusal; see the Fix section.\n- **A shared op-cert is acceptable.** The server signing under the box's existing opcert\n  environment (ADR 0104 §3, Option A) is the accepted design. The separate observation that\n  the environment holds no public key, so `verify_signature` returns `foreign_key`, is tracked\n  as `dire-expectable-terrapin` and is NOT in scope here.\n\n- [ ] **LIVE VALIDATION — REQUIRED TO CLOSE.** `review_plan` (and `scan_spec`) called through the deployed endpoint returns a VERDICT rather than `cannot resolve ref ... in '.'`, and a certified attestation is persisted.\n      Evidence must be OBSERVED against the deployed server at\n      `https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp` and recorded in a ticket comment naming\n      the tool(s) called, the arguments, and the actual response. A passing local test is\n      NOT sufficient, and neither is a merged change: the container must have redeployed\n      and served the call. This exists because a fix here was previously reported complete\n      on the strength of a merge while the deployed behaviour was still broken.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh","reason":"Provision a blobless single-branch clone of main as the code root alongside the tickets clone, backgrounded so it cannot block exec past the readiness deadline"},{"path":"infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","reason":"Set REBAR_ROOT to the code clone so gate ops resolve refs against a real repository instead of the /app source copy"},{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"mcp_run_new must set the same REBAR_ROOT and mount so blue-green containers stay at parity with the compose service"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py","reason":"Executable coverage that the code root is provisioned and resolvable, a clone failure surfaces rather than reporting success, and the compose/autodeploy env stay in parity"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","66f0-ddc9-bf24-4fa3"],["relates_to","c67b-ece5-707e-460e"],["relates_to","d26a-8ffa-97cd-4b2a"],["relates_to","fe1f-2566-59c6-4c8f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"400f3e8f-e32f-48c6-a051-c57d3dbf9fe2","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["mcp","deploy","gates"],"ticket_id":"1eb6-65f2-5a4e-4c7b","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Attested-source LLM gates are unusable on the deployed MCP server: the container repo root has no git metadata","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0ddab002-8156-4579-b13d-197e5217ea38","c496b255-edae-48d0-94b4-35f7129e0f55","20b7c656-e87c-416e-8f63-9cbbb9b17cd2","ae31b318-8bfc-495c-8136-565d5d7273ff","ed5229e9-f8ab-415e-9380-af496634ac46","400f3e8f-e32f-48c6-a051-c57d3dbf9fe2","c93036fe-3d51-441a-8500-152635b3c614","4751870a-de36-466e-ad97-15116d484376","2bc1ec4d-71c9-4571-bc1e-c912c38fb806","de11f2d3-ed41-4cee-b7fa-0d8264f4b788","7f954c4d-19c9-4761-a2be-d49560d4b7b9","6a9cb406-16a7-4792-9852-07cace850572","85442856-ac19-48e7-9156-808bab47b0af","7a825e60-c311-4461-8bd6-5c97319bc86a","a793823e-1507-4734-990e-8fc193cf9e28","b965b913-5a88-4039-839d-f974c21cb80e","29f6cee0-4cc8-4ee8-99e1-d9b8461b2991"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787863495612720002,"uuid":"e053b465-5eb5-460e-89a8-a14eb254764a"}